`onSuccess` here receives the submission result from `ObjectForm`, not the raw form values. Passing `handleSubmit` (which expects form values) will mis-handle the argument. Consider renaming to `onSuccess`/`onSubmitted` and updating the handler signature to accept the result only, or use a different hook point if you need access to the form values.
```suggestion
              onSuccess: (result) => {
                handleSubmit(result);
              },
```

FormAnalytics is new and currently has no tests. Add coverage for fill rate computation and conditional rendering of the daily submissions chart and field completion section (including empty/undefined metric arrays).
```suggestion
    const abandoned = metrics.abandonedSubmissions;

    // If no abandoned data is provided, assume a perfect fill rate only when there are submissions.
    if (abandoned == null) {
      return metrics.totalSubmissions > 0 ? 100 : 0;
    }

    const total = metrics.totalSubmissions + abandoned;
```
